{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["Into their council let not my soul come — may it be Your will that my soul not be in their counsel. For every 'al' in the Torah that refers to the future is either a curse or a blessing, a request or a command; 'al' in the sense of the past is never found. Therefore one must not interpret it as 'my soul did not come.'" "For in their anger — since in their anger." "They uprooted an ox — like: ואת סוסיהם תעקר."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:37.775182597Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}